_{1}=250 \\\\ \\mathrm{~T}_{2}=300^{\\circ} & \\mathrm{V}_{2}=500 \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{V}_{2}}{\\mathrm{~V}_{1}}=2 & \\end{array}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2015 (SA)","_marksId":"6174d21331d96ef9f6a42e2f"},{"id":51420,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"States of Matter","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Two balloons A and B containing $0.2$ mole and $0.1$ mole of helium at room temperature and $2.0 \\mathrm{~atm}$, respectively, are connected. When equilibrium is established, the final pressure of He in the system is","options":["$1.0$ atm","$1.5$ atm","$0.5$ atm","$2.0 \\mathrm{~atm}$"],"answer":3,"solution":"Since pressure of the gases are same in both the containers. Therefore the final pressure will not change.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2011 (SA)","_marksId":"6174d213a7dd073638c45bdb"}]}